  "details": "# Issue:\n\nI currently use the `UserEyeTracking` bool to enable or disable my \"Ear Tracking\", which moves my ears in the direction that I'm looking. \n\nAs I don't have eye tracking at the moment, I turned on **Disable Eye Look Tracking** and **Disable Eye Lid Tracking** which sets this value to false locally. For remote clients how ever the value stays true.\n\nThis results in my ears moving around with VRChat's automated eye look / gaze feature for remote clients.\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. On an Avatar with native face tracking add a simple toggle that uses the `UserEyeTracking` parameter.\n\n2. Launch the game with 2 clients in one instance.\n\n3. Switch into the Avatar an enable Selfie Expression.\n\n3. Go to the Main Menu > Settings > Tracking and IK and turn on  **Disable Eye Look Tracking** and **Disable Eye Lid Tracking**.\n\nIf you do this, locally your created toggle turns off, while it stays on for remote.\n\n# Expected Behaviour:\n\nWhen turning on **Disable Eye Look Tracking** and **Disable Eye Lid Tracking** no eye look or eye lid data should be sent. Thus in return `UserEyeTracking` should also be false.\n\nI understand that `UserEyeTracking` on remote is calculated based on if Eye Look or Eye Lid data is received, but since I turned off the tracking for it in the settings I would expect it to also be false.\n\n# Attachments\n\nIn this screenshot I have a cube attached to my avatar that is either on or off based on `UserEyeTracking`. While it's off locally, you can see that it's on for remote.",
